*.dylib
preview_out.jpg
native/compile_commands.json

# Vendored Halide v21 binary distribution (~540MB)
# Fetch after clone: native/scripts/fetch_halide_v21_dist.sh
native/third_party/halide/

# DNG SDK non-build artifacts (only source/*.cpp,*.h needed)
native/third_party/dng_sdk/targets/
native/third_party/dng_sdk/documents/
native/third_party/dng_sdk/projects/
native/third_party/dng_sdk/source/Makefile

# libjpeg-turbo non-build artifacts (only src/, simd/, cmakescripts/ needed)
# release/ and test/ are NOT excluded: the vendored CMakeLists unconditionally
# configure_file()s 15 templates out of them (CMakeLists.txt:1903-1912,
# cmakescripts/BuildPackages.cmake:42-166), so excluding them made a fresh
# clone impossible to configure — CI on a clean checkout exposed this on
# 2026-08-26. Together they are ~124KB of text.
# win/ is NOT excluded either, for the same reason, found on 2026-08-28 when the
# first Windows CI job ran: BuildPackages.cmake:67-121 configure_file()s
# win/projectTargets.cmake.in and win/vc/projectTargets-release.cmake.in inside
# an if(WIN32) block, so no macOS/Linux/Android build could ever reach it. 8
# files, 36KB. Excluding only the two files that fire today would leave
# win/turbojpeg.rc.in (CMakeLists.txt:700, if WITH_TURBOJPEG) and
# win/jpeg*.def + win/jpeg.rc.in (sharedlib/CMakeLists.txt:44-49, if
# ENABLE_SHARED) armed for the next option flip.
native/third_party/libjpeg-turbo/java/
native/third_party/libjpeg-turbo/doc/
native/third_party/libjpeg-turbo/testimages/
native/third_party/libjpeg-turbo/fuzz/
native/third_party/libjpeg-turbo/sharedlib/
native/third_party/libjpeg-turbo/ChangeLog.md

# Vendored LibRaw source + CMake wrapper
native/third_party/libraw/
native/third_party/libraw-cmake/
!native/third_party/libraw/PROVENANCE.md

# Vendored HEIF decode distribution (libheif + libde265, built by
# native/scripts/fetch_heif_deps.sh). Source is fetched and built, never
# tracked -- the same policy as Halide and LibRaw. PROVENANCE.md IS tracked so
# the pinned versions, hashes and configure flags survive without the tree.
native/third_party/heif-dist/*
!native/third_party/heif-dist/PROVENANCE.md

# Vendored libwebp encode distribution (static, built by
# native/scripts/fetch_libwebp_dist.sh). Same policy as the HEIF dist above:
# fetched and built, never tracked; PROVENANCE.md IS tracked.
native/third_party/libwebp-dist/*
!native/third_party/libwebp-dist/PROVENANCE.md
native/third_party/libwebp-dist-*/
# EXCEPTION: libwebp-dist-windows IS committed (Task 4, 2026-08-30 codec
# expansion) -- no machine in this project can produce Windows binaries
# locally, so unlike the macOS/Linux dist above, the Windows one is a
# reviewed, pinned INPUT, same policy as heif-dist-windows.
!native/third_party/libwebp-dist-windows/

# Vendored static libjxl distribution (+ bundled highway, brotli; built by
# native/scripts/fetch_libjxl_dist.sh). Same policy as the HEIF/libwebp dists
# above: fetched and built, never tracked; PROVENANCE.md IS tracked.
native/third_party/libjxl-dist/*
!native/third_party/libjxl-dist/PROVENANCE.md
native/third_party/libjxl-dist-*/
# EXCEPTION: libjxl-dist-windows IS committed (Task 6, 2026-08-30 codec
# expansion) -- same rationale as the libwebp-dist-windows exception above.
!native/third_party/libjxl-dist-windows/

# Vendored LLVM OpenMP runtime (committed on purpose, 756 KB - see
# native/third_party/libomp/PROVENANCE.md). The blanket `*.dylib` rule above
# would otherwise sweep the library, silently leaving a blank checkout without
# OpenMP -- which is the exact prerequisite-free build this directory exists to
# provide. The negation must name the file, since `*.dylib` matches at any depth.
!native/third_party/libomp/lib/libomp.dylib

# Session/tool scratch state (never tracked)
.claude/tmp/
.pi/

# Non-code project files (docs, logs, images, project management)
# Exception 1: the third-party license index must ship with the source. It is a
# distribution artifact required by the vendored components' licenses, and
# native/scripts/verify_raw_provenance.py fails without it.
# Exception 2: docs/images/ holds the screenshots README.md embeds. Without it
# the published README renders broken image links.
/docs/*
!/docs/legal/
/docs/legal/*
!/docs/legal/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md
!/docs/legal/LGPL-3.0.txt
!/docs/images/
/image_samples/*
!/image_samples/raw_corpus/
/AGENTS.md
/package.json
/package-lock.json

# AI coding-agent workspace files. Local development aids, not part of the
# engine, and meaningless to anyone consuming this repository.
AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/.claude/
/skills/

# Tooling / generated
.sisyphus/
.claudito/
graphify-out/
native/scripts/tmp/

# Untracked dylib snapshots used as symbol-absent test fixtures (Phase 18 Task 1)
/tmp/

# RAW corpus: binaries untracked, manifest/README tracked (Phase 17 Task 4)
image_samples/raw_corpus/*
!image_samples/raw_corpus/README.md

# TSan side-build (Foveon accel round) and root scratch probes — untracked residue, never committed
/native/build-tsan-x3f/
/scripts/

# Fetched Windows native libraries (dng_decoder_native, heif, libde265). These
# are pulled at build time from a pinned ceyx GitHub Release by Halcyon's
# scripts/build_apps.py; a fetched copy must never be re-committed as a new
# trust-on-first-use binary. .gitkeep IS tracked so the directory survives a
# clean checkout.
plugin/windows/Libraries/*.dll
!plugin/windows/Libraries/.gitkeep
